Thu Aug 20 13:53:41 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Ship shared common/ fragments in the -devel package
  (define-grammar.js, scanner.h, common.mak) next to php/ and
  php_only/, so grammar.js require('../common/...') resolves
  and installcheck no longer demands
  treesitter_grammar_src(../common).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Aug 20 08:50:40 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Convert the Python binding to the shared loader macro
  (flavor subpackages): drop %treesitter_python_build and the
  C-extension BuildRequires; %treesitter_python_install generates
  a _binding.py that loads libtree-sitter-php.so and
  libtree-sitter-php_only.so and exposes language_php() and
  language_php_only().
- Pin the python subpackage to %{name} = %{version}-%{release}.
- Suggests python-tree-sitter >= 0.22 instead of Requires,
  matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck
  does not demand a non-ring package.
- Run a functional %check parsing PHP through both shims;
  gated to suse_version >= 1699 because python-tree-sitter
  does not exist in Leap 16.0.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Jul 27 08:36:28 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package of tree-sitter-php 0.23.9:
  * PHP grammar library for the tree-sitter parsing
    framework (libtree-sitter-php.so grammar module)
  * Python binding built from the bundled bindings/python as
    pythonXYZ flavor subpackages via the shared
    %treesitter_python_build/_install macros
